<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Moon Represents My Heart</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">sold to Li Ge Records in <a href="/years/1972">1972</a>; first recorded by Chen Fen-lan, May <a href="/years/1973">1973</a>; Teresa Teng's version 19 December <a href="/years/1977">1977</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as 月亮代表我的心, Yuèliang Dàibiǎo Wǒ de Xīn</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The music of &quot;The Moon Represents My Heart&quot; is by the Taiwanese composer Weng Ching-hsi. While studying at the Berklee College of Music in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a>, he often found ideas for his music in the nearby parks and wrote them down. Back in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> he showed one of his compositions to his friend the lyricist Sun Yi.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The music of &quot;<b>The Moon Represents My Heart</b>&quot; is by the Taiwanese composer Weng Ching-hsi.</blockquote><a href="/songs/the-moon-represents-my-heart">The Moon Represents My Heart</a></li></ul></section>
